diff --git a/docs/WhateverXe.md b/docs/WhateverXe.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e2223b3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/WhateverXe.md
@@ -0,0 +1,115 @@
+# Experimental Tiger Lake Iris Xe support
+
+This integration prepares an OpenCore EFI. It does not install the macOS graphics
+stack or establish that acceleration works on a particular laptop.
+
+## Scope and versions
+
+Only physical Intel PCI IDs `8086:9A40`, `9A49`, `9A60`, `9A68`, `9A70`, and `9A78`
+use this path. Other 9Axx devices, Rocket Lake, Alder Lake, and later Xe generations
+are not added by this change. WhateverXe accepts these six IDs automatically;
+no Ice Lake spoof or `AAPL,ig-platform-id` is generated. H45/GT1 devices
+`9A60/9A68/9A70` and 96-EU configurations still need upstream hardware validation.
+
+The EFI pins WhateverXe **0.5.0 RELEASE** and **AMFIPass 1.4.1 Mod**, with SHA-256
+checksums. Install **WhateverXe Graphics 0.2.0** in the target macOS separately.
+WEX and Graphics versions are independent.
+
+| macOS | Required version | Graphics 0.2.0 target build |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Big Sur | 11.7.11 | 20G1443 |
+| Monterey | 12.7.6 | 21H1320 |
+| Ventura | 13.7.8 | 22H730 |
+| Sonoma | 14.8.9 | 23J631 |
+| Sequoia | 15.8.x | 24H32 |
+| Tahoe | 26.7 or newer | 25G241 |
+
+OpCore-Simplify's compatibility range represents EFI eligibility, not every
+point release between Big Sur and Tahoe. Its version selector works with Darwin
+versions and cannot check the installed OS build identity. Big Sur through Sonoma
+require qualified kernel identities; Sequoia and Tahoe accept servicing updates
+within their families while retaining runtime instruction and ABI checks. Check
+the upstream documentation before choosing an installer or updating macOS.
+
+## What the generated EFI does
+
+- Selects Lilu, WhateverXe, and AMFIPass. WhateverXe shares the exclusive GPU
+  group with WhateverGreen, NootRX, and NootedRed. This also applies to mixed GPUs.
+- Uses the dedicated Mod archive from WhateverXe-Graphics, pinned to commit
+  `e83018e76c0f39f0f870ff38dcc304fb357c3485`. The bundle is still named
+  `AMFIPass.kext`; only one copy is installed and enabled.
+- Stores the Mod under `OCK_Files/AMFIPass-WhateverXe`, independently of ordinary
+  `OCK_Files/AMFIPass`. Switching modes cannot select the other cache by name.
+  Missing Xe/Lilu/Mod bundles stop the build; stale pinned downloads are not used
+  as a fallback after download failure.
+- Adds `-allow3d -disablegfxfirmware`, sets `csr-active-config` Data to
+  `03080000` (little-endian `0x803`), and schedules that variable for NVRAM deletion
+  so an old value can be replaced. Existing non-Xe SIP policy is unchanged.
+- Omits legacy WEG iGPU spoof and framebuffer defaults for these six IDs, even
+  if WhateverGreen is selected manually. No universal DVMT patch is guessed.
+
+The AMFIPass dependency name is retained for existing Wi-Fi/OCLP logic. Its
+download provider changes only while WhateverXe is selected. Ordinary upstream
+AMFIPass has a different trust anchor and cannot validate the Xe Mod payloads.
+The Windows-side checks do not verify macOS code signing or load kernel drivers.
+
+## Required steps on the target machine
+
+1. Keep a known working boot method and the recovery procedure available. Check
+   BIOS settings and the qualified OS build above. Prefer DVMT Pre-Allocated 96MB.
+2. Review `EFI/OC/config.plist`: Lilu before WhateverXe, one **Mod** AMFIPass,
+   no WhateverGreen/NootRX/NootedRed, correct SIP Data and both boot arguments.
+   Remove obsolete Xe iGPU `device-id`/`ig-platform-id` overrides from any merged
+   configuration. Reusing an older EFI can preserve unrelated properties.
+3. If an old Xe System/root patch exists, restore it using its original recovery
+   method before switching to the Graphics pkg route.
+4. Boot the target macOS with the generated EFI. Download Graphics **0.2.0** and
+   its checksum from the official Releases page. Verify the checksum, open the
+   pkg in Installer, and restart only after installation succeeds. The installer
+   puts drivers and AppleIntelTGLCompat under `/Library`, rebuilds AuxKC, and
+   applies the Tahoe CoreMedia setting. It does not set EFI, SIP, or boot arguments.
+   Never put the pkg or its driver payloads in `EFI/OC/Kexts`.
+5. Verify Metal, the internal display, brightness, external outputs, and wake on
+   the actual machine. Save logs if the graphics stack fails to start. The
+   generated setup file is not proof that Graphics pkg is installed.
+
+If DVMT is fixed at **60MB**, upstream documents `-igfxdvmt` plus iGPU Data
+properties `framebuffer-patch-enable=01000000` and
+`framebuffer-stolenmem=0000C003`. Add these only after confirming that firmware
+allocation; they do not increase it. Internal brightness also requires SSDT-PNLF.
+
+Automatic Xe builds that also require OCLP root patches stop with an explanatory
+error. This check runs after Wi-Fi/audio selection, so newly introduced root-patch
+requirements are caught too. Prefer itlwm or a suitable native AirportItlwm fork
+for Wi-Fi, and SimpleHDA where offered for Tahoe audio. Existing non-Xe OCLP
+selection continues to use ordinary AMFIPass.
+
+If other devices still require OCLP root patches, a manual integration needs the
+**b00t0x custom OCLP build** with the same Mod signing chain, including matching
+restoration payloads. Upstream OCLP payloads and Xe Mod payloads cannot both be
+validated by one ordinary AMFIPass. This integration does not replace or run
+OCLP, convert its payloads, or validate mixed root-patch configurations. Do not
+bypass the automatic-build guard by mixing upstream Wi-Fi payloads with the Mod.
+
+Mixed-GPU acceleration and routing are not configured by this Xe mode. An MX450
+remains unsupported; adding Xe support does not add an NVIDIA driver. Some
+DisplayPort/USB-C reconnections can freeze the system. Full sleep/wake, high
+resolutions, and every panel/backlight wiring are not validated. FairPlay is
+unsupported. Retain the official uninstall/recovery instructions for rollback.
+
